<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 148 0 R
/E (At FON, sustainability awareness and motivation are supported through both academic work and practical student activities.)
/Pg 12 0 R
/K [4]
>>
endobj
194 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 148 0 R
/E (Sustainability is integrated into teaching across all study levels. At the bachelor level, you can explore environmental and sustainability topics through courses such as Environmental Management, Eco-Marketing, Design for the Environment, and Environmental Quality Systems. At the master level, the offer expands to subjects including Integrated Environmental Management, Sustainable Development, Circular Economy - Principles and Concepts, Environmental Risk Management, Environmental Change Management and Resource Economics, Environmental Product Suitability and Energy Efficiency, Energy Efficiency Management Systems, Environmental Management Systems, and Models of Social Responsibility. At the doctoral level, you can further develop advanced knowledge through courses such as Environmental Management - Selected Topics, and Medical Waste Management. Together, these courses allow you to approach sustainability from managerial, technological, economic, and social perspectives and to connect academic learning with practical environmental challenges.)
/Pg 12 0 R
/K [5]
>>
endobj
