203 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 149 0 R
/E (Tree planting has become a valued annual tradition at FON, bringing together students, staff, partners, and guests, around a simple but meaningful environmental action. Each year, new trees are planted at the faculty grounds as part of activities dedicated to Earth Day and sustainable development. Beyond improving the surrounding space, the initiative raises awareness of the importance of biodiversity, urban greenery, and long-term care for the environment. It also gives the FON community an opportunity to turn sustainability from an academic topic into a visible, shared, and lasting contribution. The tree is then taken care of by the Faculty members and students all year long. You are also encouraged to take part in yearly tree-planting organized by CEMOR, environmental workshops, volunteering actions, and organized visits to events such as the Science Picnic, where sustainability topics are presented in an engaging and interactive way to the youngest population. These activities help students connect environmental knowledge with everyday choices, teamwork, creativity, and community action, showing that sustainability is not only something to study, but also something to experience and practice.)
/Pg 13 0 R
/K [4 524 0 R 6 525 0 R 8 526 0 R 10]
>>
endobj
