353 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 156 0 R
/E (Food is an important part of our environmental footprint, but sustainable eating does not have to be expensive, complicated, or based on a perfect diet. For students in Belgrade, it can begin with practical choices: eating more plant-based meals, reducing food waste, choosing seasonal produce, carrying reusable containers, and buying only as much food as can realistically be eaten. Traditional Serbian meals based on beans, lentils, peas, potatoes, cabbage, peppers, grains, soups, and seasonal salads can also provide affordable and satisfying alternatives to meals centred on meat.)
/Pg 20 0 R
/K [30]
>>
endobj
